      "id": "BHM-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-archimedean-schwartz-coordinates",
      "title": "Archimedean real coordinate realization, Haar Jacobian multipliers, Schwartz decay, and low-rank closure",
      "statement": "Let E/F be a CM extension over a totally real number field F with [E:F] = 2, and let n, M ∈ ℕ with total real dimension N = 2 n M [F:ℚ]. (1) Composing an F-basis of E with the archimedean coordinate isomorphism A_∞ ≃ ℝ^[F:ℚ] yields an additive homeomorphism e_V : (A_∞ ⊗_F E)^(n × M) ≃ₜ ℝ^N and a continuous operator-valued map L : M_n(A_∞ ⊗_F E) → ℬ(ℝ^N, ℝ^N) intertwining right matrix multiplication: e_V(X g) = L(g)(e_V(X)). (2) For additive Haar measures μ on (A_∞ ⊗_F E)^(n × M) and ν on Herm_n(A_∞ ⊗_F E), there exist continuous functions A, C : GL_n(A_∞ ⊗_F E) → ℝ_(>0) satisfying (X ↦ X g)_* μ = A(g) μ and (S ↦ g^* S g)_* ν = C(g) ν. (3) Every Schwartz function g ∈ 𝒮(ℝ^N, ℂ) satisfies |g(y)| ≤ B_k (1 + ‖y‖)^(−k) for every k ∈ ℕ, with B_k = 2^k sup_(m ≤ (k,0)) p_m(g). Transporting an archimedean Schwartz function φ = g ∘ e_V and the Gram-fibre measures m_S along e_V, and pulling back along local continuous congruence sections h(S)^* s₀ h(S) = S on an open neighborhood of any nondegenerate c ∈ Herm_n(A_∞ ⊗_F E), supplies the continuous invertible operators L(h(S)), L(h(S)⁻¹) and continuous positive Radon–Nikodym Jacobian ratio C(h(S)) A(h(S))⁻¹ governing (e_V)_* m_S = C(h(S)) A(h(S))⁻¹ · L(h(S))_* ((e_V)_* m_(s₀)). Combining this archimedean Schwartz fibre continuity with the binary unit mass bound and Euler-product integrability closes the low-rank Siegel densities pillar.",
      "hypotheses": "CM extension E/F with F totally real, integers n, M ≥ 0, nondegenerate M × M Hermitian matrix J over E, additive Haar measures μ on (A_∞ ⊗_F E)^(n × M) and ν on Herm_n(A_∞ ⊗_F E) with associated archimedean Gram-fibre family m_S, archimedean Schwartz function φ represented as g ∘ e_V with g ∈ 𝒮(ℝ^N, ℂ), and local continuous congruence sections on open neighborhoods of invertible Hermitian matrices.",
      "correspondence": "Additivity and continuity over ℝ upgrade right matrix multiplication on (A_∞ ⊗_F E)^(n × M) to a continuous family of bounded real-linear operators L(g) on ℝ^N, while open-positivity of additive Haar measures ensures strict positivity of the continuous scaling factors A(g) and C(g). Composing L and C · A⁻¹ with local continuous congruence sections h(S) matches the abstract continuity input on ℝ^N, and feeding the resulting archimedean Schwartz fibre continuity into the low-rank assembly closes the entire low-rank Siegel densities theorem.",
      "dependencies": [
        "BHM-02"
      ],
